1
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:04,578
There's your teddy bear, Max.

2
00:00:04,578 --> 00:00:16,056
He just loves that teddy bear

3
00:00:16,056 --> 00:00:18,868
that Grandpa Philip bought for him.

4
00:00:18,868 --> 00:00:29,780
I took him to Philip's office yesterday for a checkup.

5
00:00:29,780 --> 00:00:59,272
You should have seen the look on his face

6
00:00:59,272 --> 00:01:10,453
when Molly gave him the injection. Molly

7
00:01:10,453 --> 00:01:12,601
Oh, did he cry?

8
00:01:12,601 --> 00:01:13,731
No.

9
00:01:13,731 --> 00:01:19,982
My dear little boy just looked up at me as if to say,

10
00:01:19,982 --> 00:01:25,383
"Mama, what are they doing to me? Help!" “

11
00:01:25,383 --> 00:01:26,361
How did you feel?

12
00:01:26,361 --> 00:01:27,647
Tell the truth.

13
00:01:27,647 --> 00:01:29,339
Didn't you feel terrible?

14
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:32,717
I sure did.

15
00:01:32,717 --> 00:01:35,295
I held him closely.

16
00:01:35,295 --> 00:01:38,273
I kissed the top of his dear little head.

17
00:01:38,273 --> 00:01:40,416
He looked up at me.

18
00:01:40,416 --> 00:01:46,829
He tried to smile.

19
00:01:46,829 --> 00:01:50,185
Being with him helped.

20
00:01:50,185 --> 00:01:50,985
Helped him?

21
00:01:50,985 --> 00:01:53,163
Or helped you?

22
00:01:53,163 --> 00:01:57,140
Being a mother is not easy,

23
00:01:57,140 --> 00:02:02,096
if that's what you mean.

24
00:02:02,096 --> 00:02:05,554
Speaking of being a mother,

25
00:02:05,554 --> 00:02:07,474
I've been meaning to ask you

26
00:02:07,474 --> 00:02:11,770
what you were thinking about regarding going back to work.

27
00:02:11,770 --> 00:02:13,003
I know Rita Mae called.

28
00:02:13,003 --> 00:02:16,008
I can imagine what is going through your head.

29
00:02:16,008 --> 00:02:19,161
I'm sure you can, Ellen.

30
00:02:19,161 --> 00:02:21,513
There are so many things to consider.

31
00:02:21,513 --> 00:02:24,442
One thing that makes it easier for you

32
00:02:24,442 --> 00:02:26,520
is that you have us.

33
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:29,885
Max will always have a family member to watch over him

34
00:02:29,885 --> 00:02:31,200
while you're at work.

35
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:36,477
I didn't have that when Richard and Susan were born.

36
00:02:36,477 --> 00:02:38,165
What did you do?

37
00:02:38,165 --> 00:02:43,788
I chose to continue with my career as a music teacher.

38
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:47,566
We hired a woman to watch Richard and then Susan,

39
00:02:47,566 --> 00:02:48,766
and I continued with my career.

40
00:02:48,766 --> 00:02:51,344
Do you think you made the right decision?

41
00:02:51,344 --> 00:02:53,722
I think I did.

42
00:02:53,722 --> 00:02:55,700
But when Robbie was born,

43
00:02:55,700 --> 00:02:59,268
I decided to give full-time attention to raising Robbie.

44
00:02:59,268 --> 00:03:02,808
I felt differently at that time.

45
00:03:02,808 --> 00:03:04,756
And you gave up your career as a music teacher?

46
00:03:04,756 --> 00:03:05,048
Not exactly.

47
00:03:05,048 --> 00:03:10,589
I continued to teach piano lessons at home.

48
00:03:10,589 --> 00:03:13,567
How did you feel about being away

49
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:16,545
when Susan and Richard were babies?

50
00:03:16,545 --> 00:03:19,523
I think I did the right thing

51
00:03:19,523 --> 00:03:22,901
for them and for myself and for Philip.

52
00:03:22,901 --> 00:03:24,501
We needed the money.

53
00:03:24,501 --> 00:03:25,479
Well, we do too, Ellen.

54
00:03:25,479 --> 00:03:31,800
Everything I earn helps us towards getting that house

55
00:03:31,800 --> 00:03:34,413
we want and need.

56
00:03:34,413 --> 00:03:37,391
I can't wait till he's just a little older.

57
00:03:37,391 --> 00:03:40,369
Our toy company makes the most wonderful toys for kids.

58
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:44,776
Max thanks you. Max

59
00:03:44,776 --> 00:03:45,847
I thank you.

60
00:03:45,847 --> 00:03:46,825
And Richard thanks you. Richard

61
00:03:46,825 --> 00:03:52,281
Now may I please say hello?

62
00:03:52,281 --> 00:03:52,554
Hello.

63
00:03:52,554 --> 00:03:52,826
Hello.

64
00:03:52,826 --> 00:03:55,653
I miss Max and think about him all week long.

65
00:03:55,653 --> 00:03:58,237
We talk about him at dinnertime.

66
00:03:58,237 --> 00:03:59,622
Will you please try to relax?

67
00:03:59,622 --> 00:04:01,215
I've never seen you so wound up.

68
00:04:01,215 --> 00:04:05,599
You seem to be enjoying the pressure.

69
00:04:05,599 --> 00:04:07,171
The truth is, I am.

70
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:09,106
My job is not an easy one,

71
00:04:09,106 --> 00:04:11,149
but I really enjoy it.

72
00:04:11,149 --> 00:04:16,534
That is exactly what I wanted to talk to you about, Susan.

73
00:04:16,534 --> 00:04:17,819
What's the problem?

74
00:04:17,819 --> 00:04:19,083
Marilyn's career. Marilyn

75
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:22,060
Well, my choice of careers.

76
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:25,038
Choice?

77
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:28,016
My career as a fashion designer

78
00:04:28,016 --> 00:04:30,994
versus my career as a mother.

79
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:33,972
Why does it have to be one or the other?

80
00:04:33,972 --> 00:04:35,305
That's what I said.

81
00:04:35,305 --> 00:04:36,950
How's that?

82
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:39,928
Why can't you do both?

83
00:04:39,928 --> 00:04:41,741
She's right.

84
00:04:41,741 --> 00:04:42,906
Both?

85
00:04:42,906 --> 00:04:45,446
Well, that's what I do.

86
00:04:45,446 --> 00:04:46,807
I have a job, and I have Michelle.

87
00:04:46,807 --> 00:04:49,964
I take care of both to the best of my ability.

88
00:04:49,964 --> 00:04:53,271
It's not easy, but what is?

89
00:04:53,271 --> 00:04:53,471
And that's what I did.

90
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:56,418
I did both with Richard and Susan,

91
00:04:56,418 --> 00:04:59,225
and I did both with Robbie.

92
00:04:59,225 --> 00:05:01,845
I thought you stayed home with Robbie?

93
00:05:01,845 --> 00:05:02,274
I did.

94
00:05:02,274 --> 00:05:07,455
But I was lucky enough to have a career as a music teacher

95
00:05:07,455 --> 00:05:11,375
which I could continue at home.

96
00:05:11,375 --> 00:05:15,186
Why can't you work at home, Marilyn?

97
00:05:15,186 --> 00:05:16,304
You're very talented.

98
00:05:16,304 --> 00:05:17,904
Designing dresses is a career

99
00:05:17,904 --> 00:05:22,477
you could establish out of your home,

100
00:05:22,477 --> 00:05:23,334
couldn't you?

101
00:05:23,334 --> 00:05:28,776
I don't know why I didn't think of it.

102
00:05:28,776 --> 00:05:31,304
It seems so simple now.

103
00:05:31,304 --> 00:05:32,554
For a year or two

104
00:05:32,554 --> 00:05:38,029
I could stay at home with Max and do my dress designs.

105
00:05:38,029 --> 00:05:42,465
And you could make your dresses at home.

106
00:05:42,465 --> 00:05:45,165
Sounds like a great way to solve the problem.

107
00:05:45,165 --> 00:05:48,421
That could solve your problem, Marilyn.

108
00:05:48,421 --> 00:05:50,603
I'm going to call Rita Mae at home

109
00:05:50,603 --> 00:05:53,102
and ask her to come by and talk about it.

110
00:05:53,102 --> 00:05:55,086
She wants to see Max, anyway.

111
00:05:55,086 --> 00:05:58,195
I think that really answers your questions, Marilyn.

112
00:05:58,195 --> 00:05:59,875
You can do it.

113
00:05:59,875 --> 00:06:00,333
Do your designs at home--here.

114
00:06:00,333 --> 00:06:05,368
And let Rita Mae do the selling at the boutique.

115
00:06:05,368 --> 00:06:07,889
And you can both benefit financially.

116
00:06:07,889 --> 00:06:12,245
I'm going to call Rita Mae right now.

117
00:06:12,245 --> 00:06:16,703
Oh, Susan, thank you so much

118
00:06:16,703 --> 00:06:21,179
for coming all this way from the city to talk to me about it.

119
00:06:21,179 --> 00:06:22,179
I hope you don't mind

120
00:06:22,179 --> 00:06:24,157
having taken so much time away from your busy schedule.

121
00:06:24,157 --> 00:06:25,282
Are you kidding?

122
00:06:25,282 --> 00:06:27,135
I don't mind at all.

123
00:06:27,135 --> 00:06:28,802
As a matter of fact,

124
00:06:28,802 --> 00:06:33,091
I came to spend some time with my favorite nephew.

125
00:06:33,091 --> 00:06:35,091
I think you should call Rita Mae right now.

126
00:06:35,091 --> 00:06:37,749
I think your idea of working at home is perfect.

127
00:06:37,749 --> 00:06:40,127
I don't know what I would do without you.

128
00:06:40,127 --> 00:06:42,454
I'm lucky to have you all.

129
00:06:42,454 --> 00:06:45,571
We are lucky to have you, Marilyn.

130
00:06:45,571 --> 00:06:48,571
And so is Max.
